  - >-
    A requirement split into clauses (W1.1 into W1.1a, W1.1b, ...) has no text of its own: its clause records are the
    requirement, each with its own level. Read level first, then text.
  - >-
    Where SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md and this file differ, this file's level governs; the prose explains.
  - >-
    fails_if is the case that breaks the record. check says who or what finds it.
  - >-
    who_decides names who settles an open choice inside the record; none means the record leaves no choice open;
    unassigned means the choice is open and nobody is named yet.
  - >-
    The records are grouped by what happens to a memory: it is written, it is kept true, and it is read.
  - >-
    There are no fixed numbers: where a limit applies, it is a comparison that measurement decides. Rd3.1a's interim
