  - title: Keep — memory stays true, and nothing is lost
    groups:
      - id: K1
        title: The decision or fact first, then the code
        basis: 'v; d: What it is for'
        requirements:
          - id: K1.1
            part_of: none
            level: SHOULD
            text: >-
              To change behaviour that a decision or fact governs, change the entry first, then the code. Changing an
              entry's claim means superseding it (K4.3): write a new entry with `supersedes`; on the old entry add a
              `changed:` line, `status: superseded` and `superseded_by`; regenerate `INDEX.md` in the same commit
              (K6.2). Work that has to go the other way is a matter for the project's workflow, not for memory.
            fails_if: >-
