        basis: 'v: nothing lost; d: What will not be put in'
        requirements:
          - id: K4.1
            part_of: none
            level: MUST
            text: >-
              An entry is never deleted. A `superseded` entry links to what replaced it (`superseded_by`). A `retired`
              entry, which nothing replaces, gives its reason in its `changed:` line. Either keeps its old body.
            fails_if: >-
              git shows an entry file deleted, a `superseded` entry with no `superseded_by` link, or a `retired` entry
